45fc90f913dd18d6","event_uuid":"5e3e1882-c42c-476e-bd9b-d853be1c6fdf","position":{"commit_sha":"8aba777d8e01cc3f629923dc7cf413932b42cee8","position":"1786559271260028001-5e3e1882-c42c-476e-bd9b-d853be1c6fdf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5956da433d66126bd06effea05af2314ccd55c155f626dcc7e9a97ed62c638ed","event_uuid":"3bb7a567-b520-42db-bc72-79252586ff4c","position":{"commit_sha":"8aba777d8e01cc3f629923dc7cf413932b42cee8","position":"1786559272126275001-3bb7a567-b520-42db-bc72-79252586ff4c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"29412f26682108c3f8ad6c3755ad23582183dbf08c723d9865971c9d5318f635","event_uuid":"4ddb0bc0-d84f-49c0-8aa0-7f4238b61c79","position":{"commit_sha":"438dfe3071292a25eeec9238eafd12cb553c331f","position":"1786563440180596633-4ddb0bc0-d84f-49c0-8aa0-7f4238b61c79"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[],"created_at":1786186460877981001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e8993cbb-f38e-4c75-a770-170c69746917","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ad16-30a7-adb6-454a"},{"link_uuid":"4ddb0bc0-d84f-49c0-8aa0-7f4238b61c79","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9f12-c225-a850-477c"}],"description":"# Thread an explicit cap_override through run_pass1 -> shed_to_budget\n\n## Problem (verified at origin/main cc69cc1179)\n\n`ProductionBatchRunner.run` receives `req.usd_budget` as a per-plan cost cap override but\ncannot apply it. `run_pass1` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:425`) calls\n`_shed_to_budget` (`:453`, an alias for `sizing.shed_to_budget`), which computes the cap\nINTERNALLY at `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py:605` — `cap = plan_budget_cap(ctx)` — with no\ninjection point.\n\nThe two \"overrides\" available today are both wrong:\n`REBAR_PLAN_REVIEW_BUDGET` is read by `plan_budget_cap` (`sizing.py:120-130`) as the BASE and\nthen centrality-scaled (`base * (1.0 + ctx.centrality)`), so it is not a cap override at all,\nand it is a process-global env var; the alternative is a parameter, which is exactly this\nticket. So the runner currently JOURNALS the request and drops it\n(`production_batch_runner.py:142-149`: `coverage[\"requested_usd_budget\"]`,\n`budget_override_applied = False`, a WARNING) and the computed cap is used.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd an OPTIONAL `cap_override` parameter along the existing call chain\n`ProductionBatchRunner.run` -> `run_pass1` -> `shed_to_budget`, defaulting to `None`\n(= today's behaviour, byte-identical).\n\n`cap_override` is the FINAL cap in USD, used VERBATIM — NOT centrality-scaled. That is the whole\npoint of the seam: the env var's base-then-scale semantics is precisely why it is \"NOT a true cap\noverride\" per this ticket. `None` (not falsiness) selects the computed cap, so an explicit\n`0.0` is honourable as \"shed everything sheddable\".\n\nThe runner then passes `req.usd_budget` and flips its journal to\n`budget_override_applied = True`, dropping the WARNING. `coverage[\"budget\"]`\n(`sizing.py:640-648`) gains a `cap_source` of `\"override\"` or `\"computed\"` so which cap governed\na run stays observable.\n\n**Scope honesty:** the plan-review gate YAML does NOT set `usd_budget` on its `finders` batch\nstep today (only the v3 schema defines the key, `src/rebar/schemas/workflow.v3.schema.json:302`),\nso `req.usd_budget` is `None` on every live gate run and the live gate's behaviour is UNCHANGED.\nThis ticket builds the seam and makes the request honourable; it deliberately does NOT start\nsetting a budget in the gate YAML, which would be a separate cost-policy decision.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. `sizing.py:586` — `shed_to_budget(..., cap_override: float | None = None)`; at `:605`\n   `cap = plan_budget_cap(ctx) if cap_override is None else float(cap_override)`. Record\n   `cap_source` in the `coverage[\"budget\"]` dict.\n2. `pass1.py:425` — `run_pass1(..., cap_override: float | None = None)`, forwarded at `:453`.\n3. `production_batch_runner.py:142-152` — pass `req.usd_budget` into `run_pass1`; journal\n   `budget_override_applied = True` and drop the \"no clean seam\" WARNING. Update the D4\n   docstring at `:22-26`, which names this ticket as the follow-up.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `shed_to_budget` with a `cap_override` BELOW the projected sheddable spend sheds criteria\n  that the computed cap would have kept, and records `cap_usd` == the override with\n  `cap_source: \"override\"`. Its companion: the same call with `cap_override=None` is unchanged.\n- `cap_override` is NOT centrality-scaled: on a ctx with non-zero `centrality`, the recorded\n  `cap_usd` equals the override exactly (the bug the seam exists to avoid).\n- `cap_override=0.0` is honoured rather than treated as absent (the `is None` vs falsy trap).\n- Through `ProductionBatchRunner`: a `BatchRunRequest` with `usd_budget` set produces\n  `coverage[\"budget\"][\"cap_usd\"]` == that value and `budget_override_applied` true.\n- **Stub-arity population.** `run_pass1` is replaced via `monkeypatch.setattr` — invisible to\n  Serena — so the population is enumerated by grepping the symbol as a STRING\n  (`grep -rn 'run_pass1' tests/`). Exactly TWO 6-positional-arg stubs exist:\n  `tests/unit/test_pass1_finder_model.py:96` and `tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py:136`\n  (both `def _fake_run_pass1(ctx, cfg, runner, single, agent, coverage)`). Both must accept the\n  new argument. Direct `sizing.shed_to_budget(...)` callers\n  (`tests/unit/test_plan_review.py:1870,1873,1890`) pass 5 positional args and are unaffected by\n  a defaulted trailing parameter.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `shed_to_budget(..., cap_override=X)` uses X as the cap verbatim, with no centrality\n      scaling: on a ctx with centrality > 0, recorded `cap_usd` == X exactly.\n- [ ] `cap_override=0.0` is treated as a real cap, not as absent.\n- [ ] `cap_override=None` (and every existing 5-positional call) behaves exactly as today.\n- [ ] `run_pass1` forwards `cap_override` to `shed_to_budget`.\n- [ ] A `BatchRunRequest` carrying `usd_budget` yields `coverage[\"budget\"][\"cap_usd\"]` equal to\n      it and `coverage[\"budget_override_applied\"]` true.\n- [ ] `coverage[\"budget\"][\"cap_source\"]` is `\"override\"` when overridden and `\"computed\"`\n      otherwise.\n- [ ] The `production_batch_runner.py` WARNING and D4 docstring naming this ticket are gone.\n- [ ] The plan-review gate YAML still sets NO `usd_budget`, so live-gate behaviour is unchanged.\n- [ ] NO 6-positional-arg `run_pass1` stub remains: `grep -rn 'run_pass1' tests/` shows both\n      `test_pass1_finder_model.py` and `test_model_class_ladder.py` stubs accepting the new\n      argument. This fails while ANY instance remains un-updated.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/workflow tests/unit/test_plan_review.py tests/unit/test_pass1_finder_model.py tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py` passes.","env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py","reason":"cap_override parameter on shed_to_budget + cap_source in the budget record"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py","reason":"forward cap_override from run_pass1 to shed_to_budget"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py","reason":"pass req.usd_budget; drop the no-seam WARNING and D4 caveat"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review.py","reason":"cap_override semantics tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_pass1_finder_model.py","reason":"update 6-arg run_pass1 stub"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py","reason":"update 6-arg run_pass1 stub"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_production_batch_runner.py","reason":"end-to-end override through the runner"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","9f12-c225-a850-477c"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5e3e1882-c42c-476e-bd9b-d853be1c6fdf","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e907-8dbd-7627-4725","ticket_type":"task","title":"plan-review: explicit cap_override seam through run_pass1 -> shed_to_budget","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4eed46a5-6305-4585-a38b-15ee49b10cfe","e8993cbb-f38e-4c75-a770-170c69746917","d3eb5e9c-2999-44b6-aa4b-b85af7ce5263","2d287bf0-ddf3-49ae-8981-c24d8bf52aea","1a8e9b33-0a37-43ff-bce3-85ac36d88f78","5e3e1882-c42c-476e-bd9b-d853be1c6fdf","3bb7a567-b520-42db-bc72-79252586ff4c","4ddb0bc0-d84f-49c0-8aa0-7f4238b61c79"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786563440180596634,"uuid":"61b13072-ae18-4f02-b7f1-28115512add1"}